---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Setup Apple Health MCP: Google Sheet in minutes, or your own database"
  description="Apple Health MCP setup: save Health data to a Google Sheet in your own Drive in minutes, or use your own Supabase/Postgres database. Then connect Claude, Claude Code, or Cursor."
>
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <a href="/" class="text-green-400 font-bold text-lg tracking-tight hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">health4.ai</a>
    <div class="flex gap-6 text-sm text-neutral-500">
      <a href="/docs/" class="hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors">Docs</a>
      <a href="/mcp-tools/" class="hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors hidden sm:inline">MCP tools</a>
      <a href="/compare/" class="hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors hidden sm:inline">Compare</a>
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors">Home</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-14 max-w-2xl">
      <div class="text-green-500 text-xs font-mono mb-3 tracking-widest uppercase">Verified checklist</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Set up health4.ai: Google Sheet first, database if you want it</h1>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Your Apple Health data goes to a destination you own: a Google Sheet in your own Drive (the easiest option, a few minutes) or your own Supabase/Postgres database (about 15 minutes, for power users). health4.ai has no account and no server, and does not keep a copy.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Path: HealthKit on your iPhone → your Sheet or database → your AI in Claude, Claude Code, or Cursor.
        Full detail lives in <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai/blob/main/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">docs/SETUP.md</a>.
        Prefer a comparison first? See <a href="/compare/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Apple Health MCP vs Health Auto Export</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        The iOS app is <strong class="text-neutral-400 font-medium">free and live on the App Store</strong>: <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/health4ai/id6783074944" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">download it now</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-16 max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-sm mb-6 uppercase tracking-widest">Easy path: Google Sheet</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-4 text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-5">
        <li><a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/health4ai/id6783074944" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Download health4.ai</a> and open it.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong class="text-neutral-400 font-medium">Save to Google Sheets</strong> and sign in with Google. The app creates one spreadsheet in your Drive with one row per day (steps, sleep, heart rate, HRV, workouts and more). It uses the <code class="text-amber-400 text-xs">drive.file</code> scope, so it only sees files it creates.</li>
        <li>Allow Health access, then follow the in-app setup checklist. Sync History shows what was written and Your Sources lists every device and app writing to Health.</li>
        <li>Open the sheet in Google Drive. Share it with an AI assistant that has Google Drive access, or download it as CSV and give it to any AI assistant. Want your AI to query live data over MCP? Use the database option below.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs mt-4">Background sync is best-effort: iOS decides when the app runs, so tap sync in the app if you need fresh data now. If iOS shares only recent Health data, the app warns you.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-sm mb-2 uppercase tracking-widest">Power users: your own database</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-2xl">Skip this checklist if the Google Sheet is enough. Use it when you want every HealthKit sample in Postgres, queryable by any MCP client.</p>
      <ol class="space-y-6">
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">1</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Create a Supabase project</div>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Free tier at <a href="https://supabase.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">supabase.com</a>. The database option needs Supabase Auth + Edge Functions: plain Postgres alone is not enough.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">2</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Create the health tables</div>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-2">Paste and run <a href="/schema.sql" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">health4.ai/schema.sql</a> in the SQL editor. Do <strong class="text-neutral-400 font-medium">not</strong> use <code class="text-amber-400 text-xs">supabase db push</code> on a fresh project.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">3</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Deploy the ingest function</div>
            <pre class="bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-xs text-neutral-300 mb-2"><code>git clone https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai.git
cd health4ai
supabase functions deploy healthkit-ingest --project-ref &lt;ref&gt; --no-verify-jwt</code></pre>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs">Also create your Auth user (Authentication → Users) and copy the UID.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">4</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Install the iOS app and choose the database</div>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/health4ai/id6783074944" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">Download health4.ai from the App Store</a>.
              Once installed: enter Project URL + anon key, sign in, start sync.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">5</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Install the local MCP server</div>
            <pre class="bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-xs text-neutral-300"><code>cd health4ai/mcp-server
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env</code></pre>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">6</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Point MCP at your database</div>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-2">The app's <strong class="text-neutral-400 font-medium">Connect Your AI</strong> screen has copy-paste MCP config for Claude Desktop, Claude Code, and Cursor.</p>
            <pre class="bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-xs text-neutral-300"><code>DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...   # transaction pooler, database password
HEALTHKIT_USER_ID=&lt;your auth UID&gt;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">7</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Connect Claude or Cursor</div>
            <pre class="bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-xs text-neutral-300"><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "health4ai": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["/path/to/health4ai/mcp-server/main.py"],
      "env": {
        "DATABASE_URL": "postgresql://...",
        "HEALTHKIT_USER_ID": "<your auth UID>"
      }
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs mt-2">Claude Desktop / Claude Code config, or <code class="text-amber-400">~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>. An npx one-liner is not published yet: clone + Python is the supported path.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <span class="text-green-500 font-mono font-bold text-sm w-6 shrink-0">8</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-white text-sm font-medium mb-1">Ask Claude for a health summary</div>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              In Claude Code run <code class="text-amber-400 text-xs">/mcp</code> and confirm <code class="text-green-400 text-xs">health4ai</code> is connected with 11 tools.
              Then ask: <em class="text-neutral-400">"Give me a health summary for the last 7 days."</em>{' '}
              Tool reference: <a href="/mcp-tools/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">/mcp-tools</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-6 bg-neutral-900/30 max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm mb-3">Need more detail?</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai/blob/main/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-400 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Full SETUP.md on GitHub →</a>
      <span class="text-neutral-600 text-sm"> · </span>
      <a href="/docs/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Docs hub</a>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-neutral-800/60 px-6 py-8 mt-12">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-neutral-600 text-xs">
      <span>© 2026 health4.ai · Not a medical device</span>
      <div class="flex gap-6">
        <a href="/docs/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Docs</a>
        <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jefflitt1/health4ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
